{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**No.** A sub-fund of an Irish umbrella ICAV does **not** have separate legal personality. The ICAV itself is the legal person; it can sue and be sued in respect of a particular sub-fund.\n\n**Segregated liability is a separate statutory protection**, not a consequence of separate incorporation. Under the Irish Collective Asset-management Vehicles Act 2015, liabilities incurred on behalf of, or attributable to, a sub-fund must be discharged solely from that sub-fund’s assets. Assets of other sub-funds cannot be used to meet those liabilities.\n\nThus, an umbrella ICAV is **one legal entity with legally ring-fenced pools of assets and liabilities**, rather than a group of separate companies.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Recognition of that ring-fencing by foreign courts is a separate question; Irish statutory protection does not guarantee identical treatment abroad."}}
